.TH GUILDMASTER 8 "2026-09-21" "guildmaster 0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
guildmaster \- machine-wide GNU Make jobserver on /dev/guild
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B guildmaster
.RB [ \-\-tokens
.IR N ]
.RI [ "FUSE options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B guildmaster
is a CUSE (character device in userspace) server. It creates
.I /dev/guild
and serves it as a FIFO-like GNU Make jobserver shared by every build on the
machine. A client reads one byte to take a token and writes one byte to
return it. Tokens are accounted per opening process: when a process's last
handle on the device is closed, including when the process dies, any tokens
it still holds return to the pool.
.PP
It needs read and write access to
.IR /dev/cuse ,
and therefore the
.B cuse
kernel module. It is normally run by
.BR guildmaster.service .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-tokens " N\fR, " \-\-tokens= N
Set the capacity of the token pool to
.IR N ,
a positive decimal integer. Zero, signed, malformed and out-of-range values
are rejected with a diagnostic and exit status 2 before any device is
opened. Without this option the capacity is the number of online processors
plus one. If given more than once, the last value is used. This option is a
downstream addition carried by the RPM packaging.
.PP
Remaining arguments are passed to libfuse; see
.BR mount.fuse3 (8).
.SH CONFIGURATION
The packaged service reads
.I /etc/sysconfig/guildmaster
and passes
.B GUILDMASTER_OPTS
to the daemon, for example
.BR GUILDMASTER_OPTS="\-\-tokens=2" .
.SH NOTES
A token count limits how many cooperating jobs run at once. It is not a
limit on processor threads or memory.
.PP
Restarting the daemon removes
.I /dev/guild
and creates a fresh pool. Handles opened before the restart stop working and
are not counted against the new pool, so let running builds finish before
restarting.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the session ends normally, 2 for an invalid
.B \-\-tokens
value, and 1 for any other failure.
.SH FILES
.I /dev/cuse
.br
.I /dev/guild
.br
.I /etc/sysconfig/guildmaster
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gm\-run (1),
.BR make (1)
